---
import PropertyPackPage from '@/components/property-pack/PropertyPackPage.astro';
import { candidateManifest } from '@/lib/property-pack-model.mjs';
---
<PropertyPackPage
  title="Technical Working Group determination"
  description="The pending Technical Working Group determination for the SPDTF 2.0 Property Pack ontology candidate, due by the end of September 2026."
  category="Governance milestone"
  crumbs={[{ label: 'Technical Working Group determination' }]}
>
  <h1>Technical Working Group determination</h1>
  <p class="lead">
    The Technical Working Group must review the current Property Pack ontology candidate
    as-is and make an initial determination by the end of September 2026. This accelerated
    review allows the component to support time-critical government-scheme work before
    every domain working group has completed a separate review.
  </p>

  <div class="callout callout--warning">
    <p class="callout__label">Determination pending</p>
    <p>
      No Technical Working Group determination is recorded. Technical validation of
      <code>{candidateManifest.candidate_version}</code> is evidence for the review; it
      is not semantic approval, release, adoption or external recognition of OPDA.
    </p>
  </div>


  <h2 id="milestone">Milestone and boundary</h2>
  <dl class="v2-facts">
    <div><dt>Milestone</dt><dd>End of September 2026</dd></div>
    <div><dt>Current state</dt><dd>Pending; no determination recorded</dd></div>
    <div><dt>Candidate</dt><dd><code>{candidateManifest.candidate_version}</code></dd></div>
    <div><dt>Scope</dt><dd>The Property Pack component, not the whole SPDTF 2.0 ontology</dd></div>
    <div><dt>Later review</dt><dd>Domain, scheme and Interoperability working groups may propose controlled changes after the initial determination</dd></div>
    <div><dt>External authority</dt><dd>No government approval or delegated authority recorded</dd></div>
  </dl>

  <h2 id="evidence">Evidence set</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><a href="/spdtf-2/property-pack/definition-and-scope">The exact 451-item Property Pack definition and source catalogue</a>.</li>
    <li><a href="/spdtf-2/property-pack/pdtf-1-lineage">PDTF 1.0 schema and extracted-ontology lineage</a>, including the incomplete semantic crosswalk.</li>
    <li><a href="/spdtf-2/property-pack/model">The complete candidate model</a>, contextual boundaries, resources, relationships and controlled vocabularies.</li>
    <li><a href="/spdtf-2/property-pack/coverage">Candidate source-coverage evidence</a> and <a href="/spdtf-2/property-pack/validation">technical validation receipts</a>.</li>
    <li><a href="/spdtf-2/property-pack/standards">The bounded standards profile and explicit non-claims</a>.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2 id="questions">Review questions</h2>
  <ol>
    <li>Does the candidate cover the Property Pack definition needed for the September milestone?</li>
    <li>Are the proposed identities, definitions, contextual boundaries and relationships fit for the initial determination?</li>
    <li>Which qualifications or changes are required before the determined version can be recorded?</li>
    <li>Which issues may safely proceed to later domain-group review, and which block the initial determination?</li>
    <li>What use, if any, is authorised after determination, and what claims remain prohibited?</li>
  </ol>

  <h2 id="decision-record">Decision record requirements</h2>
  <p>
    Before the site may say “determined”, Governance must record the group’s canonical
    identity, delegated remit, decision owner, quorum or decision rule, evidence set,
    allowed outcome, qualifications, dissent, escalation path, date and immutable
    candidate digest. Those fields are not yet complete, so this page makes no decision claim.
  </p>
</PropertyPackPage>
